Dear Clerk to the Justice Committee,

=20

I write to inform the Committee that a Judicial Review was filed on

1 December 2025 (Zahmoul v Secretary of State for Justice & HMCTS),

challenging serious administrative failures in the handling of criminal

evidence by MoJ/HMCTS.

=20

The claim concerns the failure to log, safeguard, escalate, or account

for criminal evidence disclosed to public authorities between December

2023 and May 2025, and the failure to safeguard and review devices known

to contain source-level criminal material.

=20

The Pre-Action Protocol Letter dated 19 November 2025 remains unanswered.

The criminal evidence, transmission history, and supporting material

underlying the Judicial Review have now been placed in the public domain

and notified to the press.

=20

The evidence repository is available at:

https://github.com/nadiazahmoul/JR-Zahmoul-v-SSJ-HMCTS-Archive/tree/main/06=
_JR_Grounds_Evidence

=20

This email is sent for the Committee=E2=80=99s awareness only.

=20

Yours faithfully,

=20

Nadia Zahmoul

Claimant (Litigant in Person)

=20

